    "en": "Coordinating conjunctions",
    "es": "Conjunciones coordinantes",
    "it": "Congiunzioni coordinanti",
    "fr": "Conjonctions de coordination",
    "de": "Beiordnende Konjunktionen",
    "ru": "Сочинительные союзы",
    "hu": "Mellérendelő kötőszók",
    "pt": "Conjunções coordenativas",
    "ro": "Conjuncții coordonatoare"
  },
  "locales": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Coordinating conjunctions",
      "summary": "Coordinating conjunctions join parts of equal rank.",
      "status": "draft",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "What it is",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "Coordinating conjunctions join words, phrases or clauses of equal rank. The main ones are and, but, or, so, for, nor and yet."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "tea **and** coffee",
                "I tried, **but** I failed.",
                "Stay **or** go."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "How it works in English",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "A comma usually comes before the conjunction when it joins two full clauses: It was late, so we left. Do not use a comma when the subject is shared: She sang and danced."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "html": "<table><thead><tr><th>Conjunction</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>and</strong></td><td>addition</td><td><strong>We ate and talked.</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>but, yet</strong></td><td>contrast</td><td><strong>It was small, but comfortable.</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>or</strong></td><td>choice</td><td><strong>Tea or coffee?</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>so</strong></td><td>result</td><td><strong>It rained, so we stayed.</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
